SUMMARY:David Kaser Endowed Lecture Series Presents: Dr. Safiya Noble "AI
  and Our Future: How Artificial Intelligence and Search Engine Algorithms
  Reinforce Oppression"
DESCRIPTION:David Kaser Endowed Lecture Series  Indiana Memorial Union\, 
 Whittenberger Auditorium\, and Online Via Zoom  Friday\, October 23rd\, 2
 026 at 12:00pm  Dr. Safiya U. Noble is the David O. Sears Presidential En
 dowed Chair of Social Sciences and Professor of Gender Studies\, African 
 American Studies\, and Information Studies at the University of Californi
 a\, Los Angeles (UCLA). She is the Director of the Center on Resilience &
 amp\; Digital Justice and Co-Director of the Minderoo Initiative on Tech 
 &amp\; Power at the UCLA Center for Critical Internet Inquiry (C2i2). Dr.
  Noble is the author of the best-selling book Algorithms of Oppression: H
 ow Search Engines Reinforce Racism. In 2021\, she was recognized as a Mac
 Arthur Foundation Fellow for her ground-breaking work on algorithmic disc
 rimination.  There will be a reception with light refreshments before the
  lecture\, from 11-11:45 am.  Thank you to our Co-sponsors:  Library and 
 Information Science Program\, IUI  Luddy Artificial Intelligence Center  
 IU Libraries  The Media School  School of Education  IU Center of Excelle
 nce for Women &amp\; Technology  School of Public Health–Bloomington  D
 epartment of English  Department of African American and African Diaspora
  Studies  Maurer School of Law  Department of Germanic Studies  Departmen
 t of Classical Studies  Department of History and Philosophy of Science a
 nd Medicine  Department of American Studies
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>David Kaser Endowed Lecture Serie
 s</strong></p><p>  Indiana Memorial Union\, Whittenberger Auditorium\, an
 d Online Via Zoom</p><p>  Friday\, October 23rd\, 2026 at 12:00pm</p><p> 
  Dr. Safiya U. Noble is the David O. Sears Presidential Endowed Chair of 
 Social Sciences and Professor of Gender Studies\, African American Studie
 s\, and Information Studies at the University of California\, Los Angeles
  (UCLA). She is the Director of the Center on Resilience &amp\; Digital J
 ustice and Co-Director of the Minderoo Initiative on Tech &amp\; Power at
  the UCLA Center for Critical Internet Inquiry (C2i2). Dr. Noble is the a
 uthor of the best-selling book <em>Algorithms of Oppression: How Search E
 ngines Reinforce Racism</em>. In 2021\, she was recognized as a MacArthur
  Foundation Fellow for her ground-breaking work on algorithmic discrimina
 tion.</p><p>  There will be a reception with light refreshments before th
 e lecture\, from 11-11:45 am.</p><p>  Thank you to our Co-sponsors:</p><p
 >  Library and Information Science Program\, IUI<br />  Luddy Artificial 
 Intelligence Center<br />  IU Libraries<br />  The Media School<br />  Sc
 hool of Education<br />  IU Center of Excellence for Women &amp\; Technol
 ogy<br />  School of Public Health–Bloomington<br />  Department of Eng
 lish<br />  Department of African American and African Diaspora Studies<b
 r />  Maurer School of Law<br />  Department of Germanic Studies<br />  D
 epartment of Classical Studies<br />  Department of History and Philosoph
 y of Science and Medicine<br />  Department of American Studies</p>
